asr-000071
00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We can now proceed with the opening statement of this representation.

asr-000072
00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:46.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: This morning, in the hearing of the National Irrigation Administration,

asr-000073
00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:52.560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: nabanggit natin tatlong malaking hamon ang ating pagtutuunan ng pansin

asr-000074
00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:56.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: sa mga hearing natin para sa 2027 budget.

asr-000075
00:14:58.220 --> 00:14:59.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang Super El Ni??o,

asr-000077
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang patuloy na matinding pagbaha sa Central, Southern, Northern Luzon,

asr-000078
00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:13.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang mariing napanawagan ng publiko na may managot sa mga ghost at substandard government projects.

asr-000079
00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:20.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dagdag dito ang krisis na hinaharap ng ating mga magsasaka,

asr-000080
00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:28.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: particular sa usapin ng pagtaas ng presyo ng crudo, ng pataba, ng pesticido,

asr-000081
00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:33.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: at syempre, yung matinding El Nino.

asr-000082
00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:39.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kaya dapat malinaw ang paninindigan ng panukalang 2027 budget ng DAR.

asr-000083
00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:44.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Bawat piso ay dapat may pakinabang, may resulta, at may pananagutan.

asr-000084
00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:48.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dapat nitong tiyakin ang karapatan ng mga magsasaka sa lupa,

asr-000085
00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:54.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: palakasin ang mga agrarian reform beneficiaries, at protektahan ang lokal na food production.

asr-000086
00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Lalo na ang nagbabadyangang pagpapalakasan.

asr-000087
00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:02.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pagpapalakas, sabi nga nila, the worst ever, El Nino.

asr-000088
00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:11.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The ARS proposed new appropriation of 14.69 billion is 13% lower than its 2026 GAA budget.

asr-000089
00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:18.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yet, within that constraint, the proposed budget allocates 5.9 billion for agrarian reform,

asr-000090
00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:27.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: beneficiary development, and sustainability, including P949 million for climate resilient farm productivity support.

asr-000091
00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:29.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tama ang direksyon.

asr-000092
00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:35.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Subalit, sapat ba ang mga pondong ito?

asr-000093
00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Maganda ang pangalan ng programa.

asr-000094
00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:44.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kailangan malinaw kung ano ang aktual na mayahatid ng climate resilient farm productivity support

asr-000095
00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:47.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: para sa mga agrarian reform beneficiaries.

asr-000096
00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:52.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At ang resultang inaasahan natin, tunay na pagunlad ng ating mga sakahan,

asr-000097
00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:57.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: mas protektibong, mas matatag, at mas kumikita.

asr-000099
00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sa panahon din ng matinding panawagan para sa pananagutan,

asr-000100
00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:08.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: iginigiit din natin na bawat pasilidad, negosyo, at benepisyaryo na suportado ng DAR

asr-000101
00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:15.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ay madaling ma-verify, ma-geotag, bukas sa publiko ang mga kontrata at impormasyon.

asr-000102
00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:21.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dumaan din sa independent inspection at napapatunayan aktual at umiiral at gumagana.

asr-000103
00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:27.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi kikilalanin ng climate shocks, ikanga, ang katiwalian, kapababayaan,

asr-000104
00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:31.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: umabagal na burokrasya, hindi rin mapapalitan ng imports,

asr-000105
00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:39.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang matatag at matibay at maganda ang output at productivity ng magsasakang Pilipino.

asr-000106
00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:43.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kaya naman ngayon, higit kailanman, kailangan ng tunay na bayanihan.

asr-000107
00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:49.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kailangan sama-samang pagkilos at tapat na pagtutulungan ng gobyerno,

asr-000108
00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:54.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: mga magsasaka, kooperatiba, lokal na pamalaan, at mga mamamayan

asr-000109
00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: para maprotektahan natin ang ating mga sakahan.

asr-000110
00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: at pagkainan.

asr-000111
00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:07.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Nagpapasalamat tayo sa ating schoolmate, Sekretary Conrad Estrella III.

asr-000112
00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:17.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Mas matanda siya ng mga ilang taon lamang, pero palagay ko nakakalamang siya sa paligo sa atin.

asr-000113
00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:26.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We especially like to mention that we are thankful to the Secretary for his full support

asr-000114
00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: for our efforts.

asr-000115
00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:30.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The Agri-Agra team with Secretary Kiko Laurel.

asr-000116
00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:36.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We have made a lot of progress in terms of interventions to support our farmers and fisher folk.

asr-000117
00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:44.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I must say, Secretary Conrad has been 101% supportive of our initiatives.

asr-000118
00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:55.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And we are thankful that because of his support, we have been able to put together the Sagip Saka full implementation,

asr-000119
00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:57.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: the executive orders.

asr-000120
00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:04.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We will now provide for greater support for direct purchases of our farmers and fisher folk.

asr-000121
00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:15.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And the approval on third reading, at least in the Senate, of Senate Bill 1990 and Senate Bill 1991,

asr-000122
00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:21.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: which is the reestablishment of the Bureau of Agriculture and Fisheries Co-ops under the Department of Agriculture,

asr-000123
00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:26.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and the renationalization of the extension workers for farmers and fisher folk.

asr-000124
00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:32.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We hope his support, mabulungan niya ang ating Pangulo,

asr-000125
00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:36.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: para ang House of Representatives, ang ating majority leader,

asr-000126
00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:43.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ay maikalendar na for third reading din sa House of Representatives ang mga batas na ito.

asr-000127
00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:51.180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Alam nating lahat, pag nasuportahan ang pagkakabuklod-buklod ng mga magsasaka at manging isda

asr-000128
00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:54.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: sa ilalim ng malakas at matibay na kooperatiba.

asr-000129
00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:56.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At nariyan ang ating...

asr-000130
00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:03.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ating infantry ng mga agriculture and fisheries extension workers

asr-000131
00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:10.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: talagang mabibigyan ng ikanga shot in the arm ang ating mga farmers at fisher folk.

asr-000132
00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:16.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: With that, again, we thank you, Sec. Conrad, for championing the cause of our farmers.

asr-000133
00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:21.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Mahalagang bagay na ikaw ay isang kasama natin sa Agri-Agra team.

asr-000134
00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And because of that, wala na po kaming tanong.

asr-000135
00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:24.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: No, diro na.

asr-000136
00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:35.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We would like to acknowledge our majority leader for his opening statement.

asr-000137
00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:36.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead, sir.

asr-000138
00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:39.340
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Thank you very much to the chairman of the subcommittee on finance,

asr-000139
00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:42.240
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: particularly on the Department of Agrarian Reform,

asr-000140
00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:45.020
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: to our chairman of the committee on finance.

asr-000141
00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:52.960
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And nandito po ako na yung araw para batiin at tulungan ang ating mga kapatid,

asr-000142
00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:57.660
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: mga kababayan, at mga napakasipag na government employees,

asr-000143
00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.660
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: from the Department of Agrarian Reform.

asr-000144
00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.060
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: First of all, I would like to thank Sec. Conrad Estrella

asr-000145
00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:06.480
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: for all the hard work that he has done for the department.

asr-000146
00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.900
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: We are colleagues in Congress,

asr-000147
00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:13.900
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and our fathers knew each other,

asr-000148
00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:15.520
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: pati lolo mo,

asr-000149
00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:20.680
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and it's just fitting to see how you have grown,

asr-000150
00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:23.440
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: not just as a legislator, but now as a member of a cabinet

asr-000151
00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:27.080
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and holding the portfolio of the Department of Agrarian Reform.

asr-000152
00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:30.160
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, Mr. Chairman, rather,

asr-000153
00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:36.300
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: during the four years that he has headed the department together with USEC-Galit

asr-000154
00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:38.500
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and all the USECs here and ASECs,

asr-000155
00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:40.540
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and many of them have worked in different capacities,

asr-000156
00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:48.400
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: they have continuously assisted our farmers and agrarian reform beneficiaries

asr-000157
00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:51.720
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: all over the country, particularly sa Bukidnon po.

asr-000158
00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:56.360
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Napakasaya nila po doon sa Department of Agrarian Reform.

asr-000159
00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:57.340
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: As a matter of fact,

asr-000160
00:21:57.340 --> 00:22:00.120
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: magpapayabang ako ng konti, Chairman.

asr-000161
00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:07.620
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Bukidnon is the province with the highest GDP participation in agri.

asr-000162
00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:11.080
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: We're three times larger than the second province.

asr-000163
00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:12.880
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I think Isabela yata yung second province.

asr-000164
00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:22.240
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Bukidnon, contributing pineapples, bananas, sugar, corn, poultry,

asr-000165
00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:26.000
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: piggery, swine production,

asr-000166
00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:27.320
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and many more.

asr-000167
00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:31.260
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Many, many others in the agricultural pie.

asr-000168
00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:34.500
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Talagang ano po kami, agricultural powerhouse.

asr-000169
00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:37.480
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And about half of that, or maybe more than half,

asr-000170
00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:41.400
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: maybe 70 or 80 percent of those farmers, Mr. President,

asr-000171
00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:45.520
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. Chairman, are members of agrarian reform communities.

asr-000172
00:22:45.980 --> 00:22:47.660
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And talagang napaganda.

asr-000173
00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:50.020
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: As a matter of fact, may COA report po lumabas,

asr-000174
00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:53.880
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: may co-report last year na the roads that we built,

asr-000175
00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:55.700
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: the farm-to-market roads that we built,

asr-000176
00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:56.860
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and thank you, Madam.

asr-000177
00:22:56.860 --> 00:23:00.680
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: We actually used that many times with COA,

asr-000178
00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:05.700
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: has actually increased the income of all our farmers.

asr-000179
00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:08.300
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Kasi doon sa Bukidnon, dati talagang bukid.

asr-000180
00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.620
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Kaya Bukidnon, puro bukid.

asr-000181
00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:11.860
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Walang kasada yung mga baranggays.

asr-000182
00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:13.820
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: And then with the help of the DA,

asr-000183
00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:17.280
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: with the help of our office initiatives and the DAR,

asr-000184
00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:21.100
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: ang dami po mga in-interview.

asr-000185
00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:22.580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Ninety-eight percent, I think,

asr-000186
00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:24.980
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: ninety-eight percent or ninety-five percent of those interviewed

asr-000187
00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:26.840
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: were very happy with the projects.

asr-000188
00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:30.860
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Of DAR and DA and the DPWH to the baranggays

asr-000189
00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:33.400
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: because napataas po ang kanilang income.

asr-000190
00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:35.200
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Dati po, Mr. Chairman,

asr-000191
00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:41.080
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: four pesos per kilo yung corn sa transportation.

asr-000192
00:23:41.780 --> 00:23:43.040
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Alam nyo po, four pesos.

asr-000193
00:23:43.680 --> 00:23:48.160
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Because sinasakay po nila yung mais sa likod ng kabayo or motor.

asr-000194
00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:50.080
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Kasi wala pong kasada.

asr-000195
00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:52.540
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Ngayon, because of the intervention of the DAR

asr-000196
00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.060
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: through their farm-to-market road program

asr-000197
00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:56.440
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: together with the DA and the DPWH,

asr-000198
00:23:56.860 --> 00:24:00.720
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: they only pay now twenty-five to thirty centavos per kilo.

asr-000199
00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:03.060
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Ten-wheeler truck na po nakakapasok.

asr-000200
00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:04.720
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Ang savings napakalaki.

asr-000201
00:24:05.260 --> 00:24:09.480
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So it is really a big help by this agency

asr-000202
00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:14.420
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and it's helping us grow as an agricultural province

asr-000203
00:24:14.420 --> 00:24:18.140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and it is contributing to the GDP growth of the country.

asr-000204
00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:20.860
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Kung ma-replicate lang po namin yung ginawa po ng DAR

asr-000205
00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:23.640
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: all over the country doon sa Bukidnon,

asr-000206
00:24:24.160 --> 00:24:26.840
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: talagang walang mahirap na magsasaka.

asr-000207
00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:28.020
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So I salute

asr-000208
00:24:40.960 --> 00:24:42.640
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: these men and women of here in DAR today

asr-000209
00:24:42.640 --> 00:24:45.500
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: para madagdagan po ang budget ng DAR.

asr-000210
00:24:46.840 --> 00:24:50.440
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I have nothing else to say but good things.

asr-000211
00:24:50.940 --> 00:24:52.600
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: At baka sabihin na sobrang sip-sip na ako

asr-000212
00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:54.980
